<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Dewas Junior</h1><p class="st-meta">1728 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Dewas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The junior of the two Maratha Puar states that shared the town of Dewas in Malwa, descended from Jivaji Rao Puar.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dewas">Dewas</a> Junior shares its origin with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dewas-senior">Dewas Senior</a>: the brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tukoji-rao-i-puar">Tukoji Rao</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jivaji-rao-puar">Jivaji Rao Puar</a> received Dewas around 1728 after campaigning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baji-rao-i">Baji Rao I</a>. The Junior Branch descends from Jivaji Rao, and the two lines became separate states holding interlocking villages.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The two branches kept separate palaces and administrations in the same town and even shared the main street, an arrangement that puzzled British officials of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-india-agency">Central India Agency</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dewas">Dewas</a> Junior was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> state with a Raja, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a>, and a modest revenue.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dewas">Dewas</a> Junior merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948, which became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956. The twin palaces still stand in Dewas.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dewas-junior.jpg" alt="Dewas Junior" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: QuadrangleDinglePingle · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Dewas_Junior_(Princely_State).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1728 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dewas</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jivaji Rao Puar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi, Malvi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dewas State (Junior Branch)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=dewas-junior" aria-label="Dewas Junior on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6712 1330 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dewas Junior lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7032 1586L6991 1757M7032 1586L7364 1601M7032 1586L7364 1602M7032 1586L7064 1471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7064 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7032 1586h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7032 1586h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=dewas-junior">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
